This query uses the `AVG` function to calculate the minimum, maximum, and average distance of all aircrafts. It first selects the aid of all aircrafts with the minimum distance, then the aid of all aircrafts with the maximum distance, and finally the aid of all aircrafts with the minimum distance.
```json
{
  "sql": "SELECT 
  (SELECT MIN(distance) 
   FROM flight 
   JOIN aircraft ON flight.aid = aircraft.aid) AS min_distance,
  (SELECT AVG(distance) 
   FROM flight 
   JOIN aircraft ON flight.aid = aircraft.aid) AS avg_distance,
  (SELECT MAX(distance) 
   FROM flight 
   JOIN aircraft ON flight.aid = aircraft.aid) AS max_distance
  FROM flight
  JOIN certificate ON flight.aid = certificate.eid
  GROUP BY aid
  ORDER BY aid
  LIMIT 1"
}
```

