```sql
SELECT 
  c.first_name, 
  c.last_name, 
  SUM(i.total) AS total_gross_sales
FROM 
  customers c
  JOIN invoices i ON c.id = i.customer_id
  JOIN invoice_lines il ON i.id = il.invoice_id
  JOIN tracks t ON il.track_id = t.id
  JOIN genres g ON t.genre_id = g.id
  JOIN albums a ON t.album_id = a.id
  JOIN artists a2 ON a.id = a2.id
  JOIN employees e ON e.id = e.id
  JOIN playlists p ON e.id = p.id
  JOIN playlist_tracks pt ON p.id = pt.playlist_id
GROUP BY 
  c.first_name, 
  c.last_name
ORDER BY 
  total_gross_sales DESC
LIMIT 10;
```

This query joins the required tables to get the total gross sales for each customer. The `SUM` aggregation function is used to calculate the total gross sales for each customer. The `GROUP BY` clause groups the results by customer, and the `ORDER BY` clause sorts the results in descending order by total gross sales. The `LIMIT 10` clause limits the results to the top 10 customers.
