SELECT AVG(UnitPrice) AS AverageUnitPrice FROM (SELECT AVG(UnitPrice) AS AverageUnitPrice FROM (SELECT AVG(UnitPrice) AS AverageUnitPrice FROM (SELECT AVG(UnitPrice) AS AverageUnitPrice FROM InvoiceLine AS IL INNER JOIN Invoice ON IL.InvoiceId = Invoice.InvoiceId) AS Subquery1 INNER JOIN Track AS T ON T.TrackId = IL.TrackId) AS MainQuery
```sql
SELECT 
  AVG(T1.UnitPrice) AS AverageUnitPrice
FROM 
  (SELECT 
    T1.Track.AlbumId, 
    AVG(T1.UnitPrice) AS AverageUnitPrice
  FROM 
    PlaylistTrack 
  JOIN 
    Track ON PlaylistTrack.TrackId = Track.TrackId
  JOIN 
    Album ON Track.AlbumId = Album.AlbumId
  GROUP BY 
    AlbumId) AS Subquery
WHERE 
  GenreId IN (
    SELECT 
      G.GenreId
    FROM 
      Genre 
    WHERE 
      Genre.Name = 'Rock'
  )
ORDER BY 
  AverageUnitPrice ASC;
```

This query uses a subquery to calculate the average unit price of tracks in the Rock genre. It joins the `PlaylistTrack` table with the `Track` table on the `TrackId` column, and then groups the results by `AlbumId`. The subquery in the `WHERE` clause filters the genres to only include Rock. The results are then ordered by the average unit price in ascending order.
