SELECT DISTINCT T1.Title FROM Album AS T1 JOIN PlaylistTrack AS T2 ON T1.AlbumId = T2.AlbumId JOIN Genre AS T3 ON T1.GenreId = T3.GenreId WHERE T3.Name IN ('Reggae', 'Rock')
```sql
SELECT DISTINCT T1.Title
FROM Album AS T1
JOIN Playlist AS T2 ON T1.AlbumId = T2.AlbumId
JOIN PlaylistTrack AS T3 ON T1.AlbumId = T3.AlbumId
JOIN Track AS T4 ON T3.TrackId = T4.TrackId
JOIN Genre AS T5 ON T4.GenreId = T5.GenreId
WHERE T5.Name = 'Reggae' AND T5.Name = 'Rock'
```

This query joins the Album, Playlist, PlaylistTrack, and Track tables based on their foreign keys to find the titles of albums that contain tracks of both Reggae and Rock genres. The `DISTINCT` keyword is used to ensure that each title is only returned once, even if it appears multiple times in the result set.
