SELECT 
  player_name 
FROM 
  Player_Attributes 
WHERE 
  overall_rating > (SELECT AVG(overall_rating) FROM Player_Attributes);
```

This query selects the player names who have an overall rating higher than the average rating from the `Player_Attributes` table.
```sql
SELECT 
  p.player_name 
FROM 
  Player_Attributes p 
  JOIN Player player ON p.player_api_id = player.player_api_id 
WHERE 
  p.dribbling = (
    SELECT 
      MAX(dribbling) 
    FROM 
      Player_Attributes 
    GROUP BY 
      dribbling 
    HAVING 
      COUNT(*) = 1
  )
ORDER BY 
  dribbling DESC;
```

This query selects the player names who have the best dribbling rating. It uses a subquery to find the maximum dribbling rating for each player, and then selects the players with that rating. The results are ordered by the dribbling rating in descending order.
```sql
SELECT 
  p.player_name
FROM 
  Player_Attributes p
  JOIN Player player ON p.player_api_id = player.player_api_id
WHERE 
  p.crossing > 90 AND 
  p.preferred_foot = 'right'
ORDER BY 
  p.player_name
```

This query selects the names of players who have a crossing score higher than 90 and prefer their right foot, ordered by player name.
