This query uses the `COUNT(DISTINCT customer_id)` function to count the number of unique customers, which directly answers the question. The `DISTINCT` keyword ensures that duplicate customers are not counted.
```sql
SELECT 
  COUNT(DISTINCT C.customer_id) AS customer_count
FROM 
  Customers C
  JOIN Accounts A ON C.customer_id = A.customer_id
WHERE 
  A.date_account_opened > (SELECT MIN(A2.date_account_opened) FROM Accounts A2);
```

