SELECT 
  d.dept_name AS department_name, 
  AVG(t.salary) AS avg_salary
FROM 
  department d
  JOIN (
    SELECT 
      i.ID, 
      AVG(t.salary) AS avg_salary
    FROM 
      instructor i
      JOIN teaches t ON i.ID = t.ID
      JOIN section s ON t.course_id = s.course_id
    GROUP BY 
      i.ID
  ) AS subquery
  ON d.dept_name = subquery.dept_name
GROUP BY 
  d.dept_name
HAVING 
  AVG(t.salary) > (SELECT AVG(avg_salary) FROM (
    SELECT 
      i.ID, 
      AVG(t.salary) AS avg_salary
    FROM 
      instructor i
      JOIN teaches t ON i.ID = t.ID
      JOIN section s ON t.course_id = s.course_id
    GROUP BY 
      i.ID
  ) AS subquery)
ORDER BY 
  d.dept_name ASC;
```

This query first calculates the average salary for each department using a subquery. Then it groups the departments by their name and selects the departments with an average salary greater than the overall average salary. The result is ordered by department name.
