SELECT DISTINCT name, SUM(CASE WHEN balance > 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS checking_balance, SUM(CASE WHEN balance > 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS savings_balance FROM SAVINGS JOIN ACCOUNTS ON SAVINGS.custid = ACCOUNTS.custid GROUP BY name
SELECT a.name, s.balance, s.balance AS savings_balance, c.balance AS checking_balance FROM accounts a JOIN SAVINGS s ON a.custid = s.custid JOIN CHECKING c ON a.custid = c.custid ORDER BY (s.balance + c.balance) DESC
```json
{
  "sql": "SELECT DISTINCT 
  (SELECT name 
   FROM ACCOUNTS 
   JOIN SAVINGS ON SAVINGS.custid = ACCOUNTS.custid 
   JOIN CHECKING ON SAVINGS.custid = CHECKING.custid 
   WHERE CHECKING.balance > 0) 
  UNION ALL 
  SELECT name 
  FROM ACCOUNTS 
  JOIN SAVINGS ON SAVINGS.custid = ACCOUNTS.custid 
  JOIN CHECKING ON SAVINGS.custid = CHECKING.custid 
  WHERE CHECKING.balance = 0) 
  ORDER BY (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM (SELECT 1 FROM SAVINGS WHERE custid = custid) AS subquery) DESC"
}
```

This query uses a subquery to first find customers with positive checking and savings balances, then joins these with the checking and savings tables to find customers with no balances. The results are then ordered by the count of customers with no balances in descending order.
