SELECT DISTINCT b.name FROM Web_client_accelerator AS wca JOIN browser AS b ON wca.id = b.id JOIN accelerator_compatible_browser AS acb ON wca.id = acb.accelerator_id WHERE acb.compatible_since_year IS NOT NULL AND b.market_share >= 5
SELECT name FROM browser ORDER BY market_share DESC
SELECT Web_client_accelerator.id, Web_client_accelerator.name, SUM(CASE WHEN browser.market_share IS NOT NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS market_share FROM Web_client_accelerator AS Web_client_accelerator INNER JOIN browser AS browser ON Web_client_accelerator.id = browser.browser_id INNER JOIN accelerator_compatible_browser AS accelerator_compatible_browser ON Web_client_accelerator.id = accelerator_compatible_browser.accelerator_id WHERE accelerator_compatible_browser.compatible_since_year IS NOT NULL GROUP BY Web_client_accelerator.id, browser.name
```json
{
  "sql": "SELECT 
  (SELECT MAX(market_share) 
   FROM browser 
   WHERE market_share IS NOT NULL) AS max_share,
  (SELECT MIN(market_share) 
   FROM browser 
   WHERE market_share IS NOT NULL) AS min_share,
  (SELECT AVG(market_share) 
   FROM browser 
   WHERE market_share IS NOT NULL) AS avg_share"
}
```

This query uses the `MAX`, `MIN`, and `AVG` aggregate functions to calculate the maximum, minimum, and average market share of the listed browsers. The `SELECT` statement selects the `market_share` column from the `browser` table, and the `IS NOT NULL` condition ensures that only non-null values are included in the results.
