SELECT 
  f.title, 
  f.id
FROM 
  film f
  JOIN inventory i ON f.id = i.film_id
WHERE 
  i.rental_date < '2022-01-01' AND 
  f.rental_rate = 0.99
  AND f.rental_duration < 3
ORDER BY 
  f.id
```

This query joins the `film` table with the `inventory` table on the `film_id` column, filters the results to include only films with a rental date less than '2022-01-01' and a rental rate of 0.99, and then filters the results to include only films with a rental duration less than 3. The results are then ordered by the `id` column.
```sql
SELECT 
  a.first_name, 
  a.last_name 
FROM 
  actor a 
WHERE 
  a.actor_id IN (
    SELECT 
      i.film_id 
    FROM 
      inventory i 
    JOIN 
      rental r ON i.film_id = r.film_id 
    WHERE 
      r.rental_date < (SELECT MIN(rental_date) FROM rental) 
    AND 
      r.rental_rate = 0.99 
    AND 
      i.inventory_id < 3
  )
ORDER BY 
  a.first_name, 
  a.last_name;
```

This query selects the `first_name` and `last_name` of actors who have rented a film with a rental rate of 0.99 and an inventory of less than 3. The subquery finds the minimum rental date for each film and selects all films with an inventory of less than 3. The outer query then selects the actors who have rented these films.
