This query joins the `Products`, `Actual_Order_Products`, and `Trucks` tables to get the details of all trucks in the order of their license number. The `DISTINCT` keyword is used to ensure that each truck is only listed once, even if it appears multiple times in the result set.
```sql
SELECT 
  p.product_name 
FROM 
  Products p 
  JOIN 
  (SELECT 
     product_id, 
     MAX(product_price) as max_price 
   FROM 
     Regular_Orders 
   GROUP BY 
     product_id) as max_price_products ON p.product_id = max_price_products.product_id
WHERE 
  p.product_price = (SELECT max_price FROM max_price_products)
ORDER BY 
  p.product_price DESC;
