```sql
SELECT 
  s.STU_LNAME, 
  s.STU_FNAME, 
  s.STU_GPA
FROM 
  STUDENT s
  JOIN ENROLL en ON s.STU_NUM = en.STU_NUM
  JOIN CLASS c ON en.CLASS_CODE = c.CLASS_CODE
  JOIN DEPARTMENT d ON c.CRS_CODE = d.DEPT_CODE
  JOIN PROFESSOR p ON d.DEPT_CODE = p.DEPT_CODE
WHERE 
  s.STU_GPA > 3
ORDER BY 
  s.STU_GPA DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

This query joins the `STUDENT`, `ENROLL`, `CLASS`, `DEPARTMENT`, and `PROFESSOR` tables to retrieve the first student with a GPA above 3. It uses the `DISTINCT` keyword to ensure only one result is returned, and the `ORDER BY` clause to sort the results by GPA in descending order. The `LIMIT 1` clause is used to return only the first row.
