```sql
SELECT 
  p.Position, 
  COUNT(DISTINCT c.Club_ID) AS club_count
FROM 
  player p
  JOIN 
  club_rank cr ON p.Club_ID = cr.Club_ID
  JOIN 
  club c ON cr.Club_ID = c.Club_ID
  JOIN 
  competition_result cr2 ON p.Club_ID = cr2.Club_ID
  JOIN 
  competition_result cr3 ON cr2.Club_ID = cr3.Club_ID
  JOIN 
  competition c ON cr3.Competition_ID = c.Competition_ID
WHERE 
  p.Points < 30
GROUP BY 
  p.Position
ORDER BY 
  p.Position;
```

This query joins the `player`, `club_rank`, `club`, `competition_result`, and `competition` tables to get the required columns. It uses `DISTINCT` to count the number of players with points less than 30 for each position. The `WHERE` clause filters the results to only include players with points less than 30. The `GROUP BY` clause groups the results by position, and the `ORDER BY` clause sorts the results by position.
