SELECT 
  p.first_name, 
  p.last_name, 
  m.id AS manager_id
FROM 
  player p
  JOIN manager m ON p.player_id = m.player_id
WHERE 
  m.award_id = (
    SELECT 
      a.award_id
    FROM 
      manager_award a
    JOIN 
      player_award_vote pa ON a.award_id = pa.award_id
    JOIN 
      player p ON pa.player_id = p.player_id
    WHERE 
      pa.year = 2022
  )
ORDER BY 
  p.first_name, 
  p.last_name
LIMIT 1;
```

This query joins the `player` table with the `manager_award` table to get the award IDs for the manager who won the most awards in 2022. It then joins the `player` table with the `player_award_vote` table to get the player IDs who won the most awards. The `WHERE` clause filters the results to only include the manager who won the most awards. The `ORDER BY` clause sorts the results by first name and last name, and the `LIMIT 1` clause returns only the first row of the sorted result set.
```sql
SELECT 
  p.first_name, 
  p.last_name, 
  p.player_id
FROM 
  player p
WHERE 
  p.player_id IN (
    SELECT 
      m.player_id 
    FROM 
      manager_award 
    JOIN 
      player_award_vote 
    ON 
      manager_award.player_id = player_award_vote.player_id
    JOIN 
      player 
    ON 
      player_award_vote.player_id = player.player_id
    WHERE 
      manager_award.award_id = 1
  )
ORDER BY 
  p.player_id
LIMIT 1;
```

