SELECT 
  D.Name AS DepartmentName, 
  B.BlockCode AS BlockCode, 
  COUNT(DISTINCT R.RoomNumber) AS RoomCount
FROM 
  Department D
  JOIN Affiliated_With A ON D.DepartmentID = A.DepartmentID
  JOIN Block B ON A.DepartmentID = B.DepartmentID
  JOIN Room R ON B.BlockCode = R.BlockCode
GROUP BY 
  D.Name, B.BlockCode
ORDER BY 
  D.Name, B.BlockCode;
```

This query joins the `Department`, `Affiliated_With`, `Block`, and `Room` tables to get the department name, block code, and count of rooms on each block. The `DISTINCT` keyword is used to ensure that each block code is only counted once. The results are then grouped by department name and block code, and the count of rooms is calculated. The results are ordered by department name and block code.
