This query joins the Employees, All_Documents, Document_Locations, and Ref_Calendar tables to retrieve the ids of employees who do not have any document destruction records. The LEFT JOIN ensures that employees without any document destruction records are included in the result set. The WHERE clause filters out records where the Calendar_Date is not NULL, indicating that the employee has a document destruction record.
```sql
SELECT DISTINCT e.Employee_ID
FROM Employees e
LEFT JOIN (
  SELECT d.Document_ID
  FROM All_Documents d
  JOIN Document_Locations dl ON d.Document_ID = dl.Document_ID
  JOIN Ref_Calendar c ON dl.Date_in_Location_From = c.Calendar_Date
  WHERE c.Calendar_Date IS NOT NULL
) d ON e.Role_Code = d.Document_Type_Code
WHERE d.Document_ID IS NULL;
```

This query joins the Employees table with the Document_Locations table on the Document_ID column, and then with the All_Documents table on the Document_Type_Code column. It selects the Employee_ID column from the Employees table where the Document_ID is NULL, meaning that there is no document associated with that employee. The LEFT JOIN ensures that all employees are included in the result, even if there is no matching document. The subquery filters out documents that have a valid date in the calendar.
