  i.investor_id,
  COUNT(DISTINCT t.transaction_id) AS share_count
FROM 
  Investors i
  JOIN Transactions_Lots tl ON i.investor_id = tl.lot_id
  JOIN Transactions t ON tl.transaction_id = t.transaction_id
GROUP BY 
  i.investor_id
ORDER BY 
  share_count DESC;
```

This query joins the `Investors`, `Transactions_Lots`, and `Transactions` tables based on the `investor_id` column. It then groups the results by `investor_id` and counts the number of distinct `transaction_id` for each investor. The results are ordered by `share_count` in descending order.
```sql
SELECT 
  i.investor_id,
  AVG(t.share_count) AS avg_share_count
FROM 
  Investors i
  JOIN 
  Transactions_Lots tl ON i.investor_id = tl.investor_id
  JOIN 
  Transactions t ON tl.transaction_id = t.transaction_id
GROUP BY 
  i.investor_id
ORDER BY 
  avg_share_count DESC
```

This query joins the `Investors`, `Transactions_Lots`, and `Transactions` tables based on the `investor_id` column, then groups the results by `investor_id` and calculates the average `share_count` for each group. The results are ordered by `avg_share_count` in descending order.
```json
{
  "sql": "SELECT DISTINCT SUM(CASE WHEN transaction_type_code = 'Investor' THEN amount_of_transaction ELSE 0 END) AS total_investor_transactions, "
       "SUM(CASE WHEN transaction_type_code = 'Sales' THEN amount_of_transaction ELSE 0 END) AS total_sales_transactions, "
       "SUM(CASE WHEN transaction_type_code = 'Purchases' THEN amount_of_transaction ELSE 0 END) AS total_purchases_transactions, "
       "SUM(CASE WHEN transaction_type_code = 'Lots' THEN amount_of_transaction ELSE 0 END) AS totalLots_transactions FROM Transactions "
       "GROUP BY investor_id"
}
