This query will return the minimum, average, and maximum order quantity of all invoices for each service type. The `SUM` and `AVG` functions are used to calculate the minimum, average, and maximum order quantities, respectively. The `JOIN` clause is used to link the `Ref_Service_Types` table with the `Invoices` table on the `Service_Type_Code` column. The `GROUP BY` clause groups the results by `Service_Type_Code`, and the `ORDER BY` clause sorts the results by `Service_Type_Code`.
```sql
SELECT 
  p.Product_Name, 
  AVG(i.Order_Quantity) AS Average_Quantity, 
  MAX(i.Order_Quantity) AS Max_Quantity, 
  MIN(i.Order_Quantity) AS Min_Quantity
FROM 
  Products p
  JOIN 
  Invoice_Items i ON p.Product_ID = i.Product_ID
GROUP BY 
