SELECT DISTINCT p.Product_Name
FROM Products p
JOIN (
  SELECT Payment_Method_Code, AVG(Product_Price) as avg_price
  FROM Ref_Payment_Methods
  GROUP BY Payment_Method_Code
) pm
ON p.Product_Price > pm.avg_price
WHERE pm.avg_price IS NOT NULL;
```

This query joins the `Products` table with a derived table that calculates the average price of each payment method. It then selects the `Product_Name` column from the `Products` table where the price is greater than the average price of the payment methods. The `NOT NULL` clause ensures that only distinct products are returned.
```sql
SELECT 
  p.Product_Name, 
  p.Product_Price
FROM 
  Products p
WHERE 
  p.Product_Price = (
    SELECT 
      MAX(p2.Product_Price)
    FROM 
      Products p2
    JOIN 
      Ref_Payment_Methods rm ON p2.payment_method_code = rm.payment_method_code
    JOIN 
      Addresses a ON p2.Address_ID = a.Address_ID
    WHERE 
      a.City_Town = 'Most Expensive'
  )
ORDER BY 
  p.Product_Price DESC;
```

