SELECT 
  D.Document_Type_Code,
  D.Document_Type_Name,
  D.Document_ID,
  D.Document_Date,
  D.Document_Name,
  D.Document_Description,
  D.Other_Details
FROM 
  Documents D
  JOIN Documents_with_Expenses DW ON D.Document_ID = DW.Document_ID
  JOIN Ref_Budget_Codes BC ON DW.Budget_Type_Code = BC.Budget_Type_Code
  JOIN Projects P ON D.Project_ID = P.Project_ID
  JOIN Ref_Document_Types RT ON D.Document_Type_Code = RT.Document_Type_Code
WHERE 
  D.Document_Type_Name = 'Budget Type'
  AND D.Document_Date >= (SELECT MIN(Document_Date) FROM Documents_with_Expenses)
  AND D.Document_Date <= (SELECT MAX(Document_Date) FROM Documents_with_Expenses)
ORDER BY 
  D.Document_Type_Code, D.Document_Date;
```

This query joins the `Documents`, `Documents_with_Expenses`, `Ref_Budget_Codes`, and `Ref_Document_Types` tables to retrieve the required columns. It filters the results to only include documents with a budget type name of 'Budget Type' and dates between the minimum and maximum dates of expenses. The results are then ordered by document type
