GROUP BY 
  D.Document_Type_Code
ORDER BY 
  D.Document_Type_Code;
```

This query joins the `Documents_with_Expenses`, `Documents`, and `Ref_Budget_Codes` tables to get the count of documents for each budget type. The `DISTINCT` keyword ensures that each budget type is only counted once, even if there are multiple documents of the same type. The `COUNT(DISTINCT D.Document_Type_Code)` counts the number of unique document types. The results are then grouped by `Document_Type_Code` and ordered by `Document_Type_Code`.
