This query joins the `Parties` table with the `Party_Addresses` table on the `party_id` column, and then with the `Addresses` table on the `address_id` column. It filters the results to only include rows where the `email` column matches the provided value. The results are then ordered by the `payment_method_code` and `party_phone` columns, and limited to the first row.
```sql
SELECT 
  i.first_name, 
  i.last_name, 
  p.email
FROM 
  Individuals i
  JOIN 
  Parties p ON i.individual_id = p.individual_id
  JOIN 
  Party_Addresses pa ON p.party_id = pa.party_id
